    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Gunnar Henderson** (71.30) and **Drake Baldwin** (70.50) stand out as our most potent options. Despite a lineup still pending for **Gunnar Henderson**, his matchup against J. Lopez (xERA 4.74) is highly favorable; he benefits from a massive 18% boost due to the opposing pitcher\u2019s skill profile and a park factor that plays nicely into his power upside. **Drake Baldwin** is equally compelling batting out of the lead-off spot. While there is a 33% risk of rain, his matchup against Sugano (xERA 4.91) is the weakest opposing pitching performance on our card, and his 10% efficiency bump for hitting atop the order makes him an essential start, even with the weather uncertainty.\n\nThe tightest decision on the roster involves the outfield and utility spots, where **Heliot Ramos** (60.81) barely secures a start over the likes of **Kyle Tucker** (57.70) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (57.26). **Heliot Ramos** captures a \"Strong\" designation by navigating a neutral platoon advantage against Sandoval, while **Kyle Tucker** faces a suppressed score due to a difficult matchup against D. Anderson (xERA 3.41), which offsets his base projections. We are monitoring **Coby Mayo** (65.57) closely; although he is currently projected in the #7 hole, his score remains robust against J. Lopez, suggesting he remains a high-floor play even if he does not move up in the order.\n\nLooking at the bench, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** remains the most frustrating exclusion. As he is not confirmed in the starting lineup for his respective club, he carries a zero-score, forcing us to lean on the higher-efficiency metrics of our active squad. We continue to navigate a depleted reserve pool with **Andy Pages**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Jacob Wilson** sidelined on the IL, while prospects like **Nasim Nunez**, **Josh Jung**, **Dominic Smith**, **Curtis Mead**, **Wade Meckler**, **Luis Lara**, and **Tommy White** remain ready should injury or rest days necessitate a pivot. With stolen bases at a premium, we are effectively playing the efficiency margins, keeping a close eye on **Sam Antonacci** (58.50), whose lead-off role provides the necessary speed production to keep our team totals competitive.",
